<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Mark-and-sweep =C4=91=C6=B0=E1=
=BB=A3c ph=C3=A1t tri=E1=BB=83n =C4=91=E1=BB=83 overcome fundamental limita=
tions c=E1=BB=A7a reference counting. Algorithm n=C3=A0y based tr=C3=AAn m=
=E1=BB=99t insight brilliant: <strong>thay v=C3=AC track references, h=C3=
=A3y track reachability</strong>.</p>
<h4 class=3D"text-base font-bold text-text-100 mt-1">Historical Context: S=
=E1=BB=B1 Ph=C3=A1t Tri=E1=BB=83n</h4>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1960</strong>: John McCa=
rthy developed mark-and-sweep cho LISP
<strong>1970s</strong>: Algorithm =C4=91=C6=B0=E1=BB=A3c refined v=C3=A0 op=
